  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "e9a03fcc-203a-4332-91c9-09de4ab43098",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#Data Exploration – Patterns and Correlations\n",
    "#The following patterns were observed from the graphs:\n",
    "#1. Pregnancies: Most individuals have a low number of pregnancies.\n",
    "#2. Glucose: Most glucose values are concentrated between 80 and 140.\n",
    "#3. Blood Pressure: Most values are around 60–80, with some zero values.\n",
    "#4. Skin Thickness: The distribution contains many zero values.\n",
    "#5. Insulin: The data is right-skewed, with several unusually high values.\n",
    "#6. BMI: Most values are concentrated between 25 and 40.\n",
    "#7. Diabetes Pedigree Function: Most values are low, with a few higher values.\n",
    "#8. Age: Most individuals are relatively young.\n",
    "#9. Outcome: More individuals belong to the non-diabetic class than the diabetic class.\n",
    "#Overall: The graphs show outliers, skewed distributions, and some positive relationships between features, such as BMI and Skin Thickness. These patterns help understand the data before model building."
   ]
  },
